msgid "Intermolecular interaction energies"
msgstr "分子间相互作用能"

msgid ""
"Counterpoise corrected (or uncorrected) intermolecular interaction energies "
"can be computed automatically using the ``INTERACT`` procedure:"
msgstr "可以使用 ``INTERACT`` 过程自动计算经均衡校正（或未经校正）的分子间相互作用能："

msgid ""
"The INTERACT command can follow any input for a complete energy calculation "
"and then computes the interaction energy for the last computed energy "
"method. Alternatively, the energy calculation can be defined in a procedure."
" In this case, the procedure must contain input for a complete energy "
"calculation, including the orbital optimization."
msgstr ""
"INTERACT "
"命令可以跟在任何完整能量计算的输入之后，然后为最后计算的能量方法计算相互作用能。或者，能量计算可以在一个过程中定义。在这种情况下，该过程必须包含完整能量计算的输入，包括轨道优化。"

msgid ""
"Dimer and monomer calculations must be carried out with the same symmetry. "
"Note that the symmetry in the monomer CP calculations is sometimes lower "
"than that of the dimer. The program checks the symmetry and stops with a "
"message if a lower symmetry needs to be specified."
msgstr ""
"二聚体和单体计算必须使用相同的对称性进行。请注意，单体 CP "
"计算中的对称性有时低于二聚体的对称性。程序会检查对称性，如果需要指定较低的对称性，则会停止并显示消息。"

msgid "The following *options* are available:"
msgstr "以下 *选项* 可用："

msgid "References"
msgstr "参考文献"

msgid ""
"Andreas Hansen, Peter J. Knowles, and Hans-Joachim Werner, Accurate "
"Calculation of Noncovalent Interactions Using PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 in Molpro `J."
" Phys. Chem. A <https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.jpca.5c02316>`__ "
"129, 4812-4833 (2025)."
msgstr ""
"Andreas Hansen, Peter J. Knowles, and Hans-Joachim Werner, 在Molpro中使用PNO-"
"LCCSD(T)-F12精确计算非共价相互作用 `J. Phys. Chem. A "
"<https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.jpca.5c02316>`__ 129, 4812-4833 "
"(2025)."

msgid "``INTERACT, options``"
msgstr "``INTERACT, options``"

msgid ""
"``*  DO_CP[=value] If zero, do not compute CP-correction (default "
"DO_CP=1).\\\\`` \\* ``DO_NOCP``\\ [=\\ *value*] Calculate non-cp corrected "
"interaction energy (**default  DO_NOCP=0**). Note: this does not work with "
"region calculations. \\* ``PROC[NAME]``\\ =\\ *procname* Use the given "
"procedure to carry out the energy calculations. \\* ``STARTCMD``\\ =\\ "
"*command* The energy calculation is defined by all input starting at this "
"command until the **INTERACT** command. \\* ``VARIABLE=``\\ =\\ *name* Use "
"energies provided in variable *name* to compute interaction energies. This "
"can be a vector of values. If not given, a selection of energy variables is "
"determined automatically. \\* ``UNIT``\\ =\\ *unit* Specifies a unit for the"
" printed interaction energies. Can be KCAL, KJ, AU, or CM (**default "
"KCAL/MOL**). \\* ``FAC``\\ =\\ *[factors]* Factors for each monomer. For "
"example, if the two monomers in a dimer calculation are symmetry equivalent,"
" one can give ``FAC=[2,0]``, which means that the second monomer calculation"
" is skipped. The sum of the factors must equal the number of monomers. ``* "
"CHARGE=[charges] Charges for each monomer (default zero)\\\\`` \\* "
"``SPIN``\\ =\\ *[spins]* Spins for each monomer. This means the number of "
"singly occupied orbitals, i.e. 2 :math:`m_s`. The spin of the complex is "
"assumed to be the sum of the monomer spins. \\* ``FILE|SAVE``\\ =\\ "
"*filename* Save intermediate results in the given file. If the file is "
"present, the program automatically restarts from it (unless ``NEW`` is "
"given, see below). New results for later restarts are written to this file. "
"From Molpro 2025.3 it is possible to add options ``DO_CP`` or ``RELAX`` in a"
" restart after a completed CP calculation. \\* ``START[FILE]``\\ =\\ "
"*filename* File used for restart (**default FILE**). This can be used to "
"avoid overwriting of the restart data, for example in connection with "
"``REPEAT`` (see below). When ``STARTFILE`` and ``FILE`` are present and "
"``FILE`` is empty (new), ``REPEAT`` is implied. If ``FILE`` is not empty, "
"restart data are taken from it. \\* ``NEW`` A new restart file is created. "
"If it exists, it is overwritten. \\* ``REPEAT`` The calculation is repeated "
"even if restart data are found. For example, one could first do the DF-HF "
"and DF-CABS calculations, and subsequently carry out PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 "
"calculations. The difference to ``NEW`` is that a restart is carried out, "
"and for example orbital records, monomers, and symmetry are remembered. \\* "
"``USE_LOG[FILE]`` If this option is given, the outputs are written to the "
"logfile. \\* ``MAXCALC``\\ =\\ *value* Only the given number of molecules is"
" computed. This requires ``FILE`` to be present to save and restart the "
"data. For example, in a new calculation ``MAXCALC=1`` would only compute the"
" dimer energy. The option can be used to split an otherwise exceedingly long"
" calculation into several smaller ones. \\* ``SCALE``\\ =\\ *factor* Two "
"atoms are considered as bonded if the distance between them is smaller than "
"sum of the atomic radii multiplied by this factor. This can affect the "
"automatic detection of the monomers (**default 1.2**). \\* ``NOSYM`` Forces "
"the calculation to be carried out without symmetry. \\* ``RECORD``\\ =\\ "
"*record* Dump record number for the dimer calculation. The records for each "
"subsequent monomer calculations are incremented by one. Normally, the "
"program determines the record number automatically and this option should "
"normally not be given. \\* ``MERGE``\\ =\\ *[list of molecules]* Merge the "
"specified molecules to one monomer. The numbering of molecules is as they "
"are given in the total complex. For example, if the complex consists of 3 "
"monomers (as, e.g. GGG in the L7 test set), one can merge the second and "
"third to one using ``MERGE=[2,3]``. Then the interaction energy of G+GG will"
" be computed."
msgstr ""
"``*  DO_CP[=value] 若为零，则不计算 CP 校正（默认 DO_CP=1）。\\\\`` \\* ``DO_NOCP``\\ [=\\ "
"*\\ value\\ *] 计算非 CP 校正的相互作用能（**默认 DO_NOCP=0**）。注意：这不适用于区计算。 \\* "
"``PROC[NAME]``\\ =\\ *procname* 使用给定的过程执行能量计算。 \\* ``STARTCMD``\\ =\\ *\\ "
"command\\ * 能量计算由从该命令开始直到 **INTERACT** 命令的所有输入定义。 \\* ``VARIABLE=``\\ =\\ "
"*name* 使用变量 *name* 中提供的能量来计算相互作用能。这可以是一个值的向量。若未给出，则自动确定能量变量的选择。 \\* "
"``UNIT``\\ =\\ *\\ unit\\ * 指定打印的相互作用能的单位。可以是 KCAL、KJ、AU 或 CM（**默认 "
"KCAL/MOL**）。 \\* ``FAC``\\ =\\ *[factors]* "
"每个单体的因子。例如，如果二聚体计算中的两个单体是对称等价的，可以给出 ``FAC=[2,0]``\\ "
"，这意味着跳过第二个单体的计算。因子的总和必须等于单体的数量。 ``* CHARGE=[charges] 每个单体的电荷（默认零）\\\\`` \\* "
"``SPIN``\\ =\\ *\\ [spins]\\ * 每个单体的自旋。这表示单占据轨道的数量，即 2 "
":math:`m_s`。复合物的自旋假定为单体自旋之和。 \\* ``FILE|SAVE``\\ =\\ *filename* "
"将中间结果保存在给定的文件中。如果文件存在，程序会自动从该文件重启（除非给出 ``NEW``\\ ，见下文）。后续重启所需的新结果会写入此文件。从 "
"Molpro 2025.3 起，可以在完成 CP 计算后的重启中添加选项 ``DO_CP`` 或 ``RELAX``\\ 。 \\* "
"``START[FILE]``\\ =\\ *\\ filename\\ * 用于重启的文件（**默认 FILE**）。这可用于避免覆盖重启数据，例如与"
" ``REPEAT``（见下文）结合使用。当 ``STARTFILE`` 和 ``FILE`` 存在且 ``FILE`` 为空（新）时，隐含 "
"``REPEAT``。如果 ``FILE`` 不为空，则从中读取重启数据。 \\* ``NEW`` 创建新的重启文件。如果已存在，则被覆盖。 \\* "
"``REPEAT`` 即使找到重启数据也重复计算。例如，可以先进行 DF-HF 和 DF-CABS 计算，然后执行 PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 "
"计算。与 ``NEW`` 的区别在于会执行重启，并且例如轨道记录、单体和对称性会被保留。 \\* ``USE_LOG[FILE]`` "
"如果给出此选项，输出将写入日志文件。 \\* ``MAXCALC``\\ =\\ *\\ value\\ * 仅计算给定数量的分子。这要求存在 "
"``FILE`` 以保存和重启数据。例如，在新计算中 ``MAXCALC=1`` "
"将只计算二聚体能量。该选项可用于将原本极长的计算拆分为若干个较小的计算。 \\* ``SCALE``\\ =\\ *factor* "
"如果两个原子之间的距离小于原子半径之和乘以该因子，则认为它们成键。这会影响单体的自动检测（\\ **默认 1.2**\\ ）。 \\* "
"``NOSYM`` 强制计算在无对称性下进行。 \\* ``RECORD``\\ =\\ *record* "
"二聚体计算的转储记录号。每个后续单体计算的记录号递增一。通常，程序会自动确定记录号，一般不应给出此选项。 \\* ``MERGE``\\ =\\ *\\"
" [list of molecules]* 将指定的分子合并为一个单体。分子的编号与它们在总复合物中给出的顺序一致。例如，如果复合物由 3 "
"个单体组成（如 L7 测试集中的 GGG），可以使用 ``MERGE=[2,3]`` 将第二个和第三个合并为一个。然后计算 G+GG 的相互作用能。"
